The support desk caches open tickets in a set so a background sweep can skip ones it has already seen.

```csharp
public record Ticket(string Id, string Subject, TicketStatus Status);

var seen = new HashSet<Ticket>();
seen.Add(ticket);

// ... elsewhere, an agent edits the subject ...
var edited = ticket with { Subject = "Printer jam (second floor)" };

bool alreadyProcessed = seen.Contains(edited);   // false
```

The sweep reprocesses the ticket every time anyone edits it. What is the modelling error?

solution.code:
function recordsEqual(members, left, right) {
  for (const name of members) {
    if (left[name] !== right[name]) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

grading.starterCode:
function recordsEqual(members, left, right) {
  // Compares every key present, not just the declared members.
  const keys = Object.keys(left);
  for (const key of keys) {
    if (left[key] !== right[key]) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

