This helper is fast in unit tests and slow in production.

```csharp
public static Summary Summarise(IEnumerable<Ticket> tickets)
{
    return new Summary(
        Total: tickets.Count(),
        Breached: tickets.Count(t => t.IsBreached),
        Oldest: tickets.OrderBy(t => t.OpenedAt).FirstOrDefault());
}
```

Tests pass a `List<Ticket>` and it is instant. Production passes the result of a database query and it makes three round trips. What is the defect, and what is the minimal fix?

solution.code:
function satisfiesConstraints(type, constraints) {
  for (const constraint of constraints) {
    if (constraint === 'class') {
      if (type.isValueType !== false) {
        return false;
      }
    } else if (constraint === 'struct') {
      if (type.isValueType !== true) {
        return false;
      }
    } else if (constraint === 'new()') {
      if (type.hasParameterlessConstructor !== true) {
        return false;
      }
    } else if (!type.implements.includes(constraint)) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

grading.starterCode:
function satisfiesConstraints(type, constraints) {
  // Only checks the first constraint and ignores the rest.
  if (constraints.length === 0) {
    return true;
  }
  const first = constraints[0];
  if (first === 'class') {
    return type.isValueType === false;
  }
  return true;
}
